      "body": "Actually, in 3.14 only the C implementation of `BufferedWriter` doesn't crash, the Python implementation does. My PR only restores the 3.14 behavior, so the C implementation does not crash, but the Python implementation still does.\n\nIs it worth trying to patch the Python implementation as well? My feeling is this usage of `BufferedWriter` is abnormal. I imagine many library facilities may crash if given `NotImplemented`?",
