      "updated_at": "2025-10-27T05:34:59Z",
      "body": "I want to make sure disambiguating crash: \"The interpreter exits with an exception / error message\" is distinct from \"There's a segfault\". In this case, the `_io` C code is misbehaved by what the interpreter loop wants: It returns non-NULL, I believe Py_None, when an exception is set when it should return NULL).\n\nGenerally `_pyio` and `_io` should match in visible behavior / exceptions (but implementations do differ between the two). In a case like this I'm less worried about them matching because it's not really a supported behavior. Best if they match but not worth a really complex PR or refactor to make that the case.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
