      "updated_at": "2025-10-27T05:38:35Z",
      "body": "I believe changing `IS_CLOSED` to preserve the sign for the error check is safe, since its only used in if-condition contexts where C's bool casting rules should apply (the PR), but would you prefer a patch like this?\n```patch\ndiff --git a/Modules/_io/bufferedio.c b/Modules/_io/bufferedio.c\nindex 5497c3d0d94..47420160213 100644\n--- a/Modules/_io/bufferedio.c\n+++ b/Modules/_io/bufferedio.c\n@@ -555,10 +555,9 @@ _io__Buffered_close_impl(buffered *self)\n     }\n     /* gh-138720: Use IS_CLOSED to match flush CHECK_CLOSED. */\n     r = IS_CLOSED(self);\n-    if (r < 0)\n-        goto end;\n     if (r > 0) {\n-        res = Py_NewRef(Py_None);\n+        if (!PyErr_Occurred())\n+            res = Py_NewRef(Py_None);\n         goto end;\n     }\n ```",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
