      "created_at": "2025-10-27T05:50:23Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-10-27T05:50:29Z",
      "body": "Yes, that's my preference. Both the `CHECK_CLOSED` macro and `_io_BufferedWriter_write_impl` call of `IS_CLOSED` could set another exception while the \"closed exception\" is set which I think isn't great (although supported / not a crash; just more exception context)\n\n---\nIt might be worthwhile to do a more general fix to `CHECK_CLOSED` because the \"IS_CLOSED\" check in it could set an exception (and evaluate to 1) than the && _maybe_ could cause it not error and return NULL itself... I haven't fully investigated that though / need to give it more thought... Also has moderate chance to break other behaviors / tests. ",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
